WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:55.850
<b>Okama Kenpo</b>

3
00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:00.540
[ROYAL SOLDIER F yelling]

4
00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:02.010
[REBEL SOLDIER A yelling]

5
00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:04.180
Are you all right?

6
00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:05.220
[REBEL SOLDIER A]
Yeah.

7
00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:09.720
[REBEL SOLDIER B]
Koza! Are you okay?

8
00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:12.190
I'm fine.

9
00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:13.160
Are you sure?

10
00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:15.390
That bullet from Nanohana is still in you.

11
00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:17.520
[KOZA]
None of that matters now.

12
00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:19.260
This is a battlefield we're on.

13
00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:21.380
We have to stay focused on what's happening.

14
00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:23.050
Got that?

15
00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:25.080
I'd like to get to one of their horses.

16
00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:26.650
If we can make our
way down this street

17
00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:29.220
and through the center of town,
then we'll be at the north block

18
00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:30.690
where the royal palace is.

19
00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:32.590
[REBEL SOLDIER B, KOZA grunt]

20
00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:34.330
What are you planning, Koza?

21
00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:35.760
Why go to the palace?

22
00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:39.460
To reach the king and
demand that he surrender to us.

23
00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:40.700
But that's insane!

24
00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:43.500
The main force of the royal army
is stationed in the north block!

25
00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:46.070
And what's more, they're led by Chaka and Pell.

26
00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:47.330
Think of the danger!

27
00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.170
And we haven't even
managed to gather

28
00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:50.750
all of our forces together.

29
00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:52.420
Don't you think it would be a better idea

30
00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:54.860
to wait until reinforcements arrive here to help?

31
00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:57.630
We can't.
It's already too late for that.

32
00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:00.030
Now come on!

33
00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:02.700
[REBEL SOLDIER B]
Wait! Koza!

34
00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:17.200
Halt! Are you aligned
with the rebel army?

35
00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:21.140
The only thing ahead
of here in the north block

36
00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:23.310
is the royal palace.

37
00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:24.740
Do you understand me?

38
00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:27.780
[ROYAL SOLDIER C]
If you aren't
a part of the battle,

39
00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:30.080
leave this area of town at once!

40
00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:31.910
[ROYAL SOLDIER A]
Hey! Are you listening?

41
00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:34.740
This place is no playground, you get it?

42
00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:35.900
[VIVI]
I know that!

43
00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:39.370
[ROYAL SOLDIER F]
Princess Vivi?

44
00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:40.940
[ROYAL SOLDIER G]
It can't be!

45
00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:42.080
[ROYAL SOLDIER H]
Is it really her?

46
00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:46.700
[VIVI]
Where's my father?

47
00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:47.830
I need him now!

48
00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.560
Well, Princess...

49
00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:51.600
[VIVI]
Never mind.

50
00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:53.740
If I can't see him, then take me to Chaka.

51
00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:57.510
There's something
that he must do!

52
00:03:58.430 --> 00:04:04.560
<b>Polka Street, South Block
Alubarna</b>

53
00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:14.820
<b>Mr. 2 Bon Kurei vs. Sanji</b>

54
00:04:22.270 --> 00:04:23.270
[SANJI]
Bastard!

55
00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:27.740
[MR. 2]
That was quite a kick.

56
00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:30.440
This one can compete with
my Ballet Kenpo moves!

57
00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:34.380
You! Out of my way!

58
00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:35.480
[SANJI]
I already told you.

59
00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:38.510
If you want to get by,
you'll have to defeat me first!

60
00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:42.150
I hope you realize all your efforts will be in vain.

61
00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:44.990
All my life I have practiced these dance moves.

62
00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:47.120
I have perfected the
dancer's graceful art

63
00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:48.890
of Ballet Kenpo
and it is unbeatable,

64
00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:51.160
even by the likes of you!

65
00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:57.800
[MR. 2]
Just give up!
It's no use trying to escape!

66
00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:02.340
Ballet Kenpo!

67
00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:11.010
[swans honking]

68
00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:18.280
My Degenerate Swan
Dance Recital!

69
00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:27.390
This dance isn't
getting me anywhere;

70
00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:29.860
it's time to settle
this once and for all.

71
00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:34.450
– Collier Shoot!
[MR. 2]
– Un!

72
00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:36.920
[SANJI]
– Epaule!
[MR. 2]
– Deux!

73
00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:39.790
[SANJI]
– Cotelette!
[MR. 2]
– Ora!

74
00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:42.490
[SANJI]
Selle!

75
00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:43.860
[MR. 2]
Un!

76
00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:45.760
[SANJI]
– Poitrine!
[MR. 2]
– Deux!

77
00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:46.960
[SANJI]
– Gigot!
[MR. 2]
– Krah!

78
00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:50.000
[MR. 2]
Ballet Kenpo!

79
00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:54.200
[SANJI]
Mouton Shoot!

80
00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:55.870
[MR. 2]
Swan Arabesque!

81
00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:08.280
[MR. 2 yells]

82
00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:18.320
[SANJI]
My Mouton Shoot...
blocked by that clown?

83
00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:21.660
[MR. 2]
My ultimate Swan Arabesque,

84
00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:24.060
stopped by that stupid,
insignificant cook?

85
00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:27.460
You've gotta be kidding me here!

86
00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:32.240
Okay, it's time to get serious.
From now on, I mean business!

87
00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:34.040
Do you hear me?

88
00:06:34.070 --> 00:06:35.570
Let's see it, then.

89
00:06:35.570 --> 00:06:36.710
Hah!

90
00:06:36.740 --> 00:06:40.740
You don't know the true extent
of my power yet, do you?

91
00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:42.580
My most impressive
feature is my ability

92
00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:44.310
to remember faces.

93
00:06:44.310 --> 00:06:46.310
Using that, I can
construct and display

94
00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:48.090
an incredible montage!

95
00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:50.980
When you see this,
you will laugh helplessly

96
00:06:50.980 --> 00:06:52.310
until you collapse.

97
00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:58.150
To begin... The world's
most ridiculous hair.

98
00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:01.320
Then, the world's
most ridiculous eyes.

99
00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.920
The most ridiculous nose.

100
00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:06.260
And then the world's
most ridiculous mouth.

101
00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:07.330
[laughs]

102
00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:09.230
Now, take a good, long look!

103
00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:14.400
Experience the grand unveiling
of the Copy-Copy Montage!

104
00:07:15.670 --> 00:07:20.940
[MR. 2 laughing]

105
00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:33.080
I'll help you.

106
00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:35.150
Stop playing dress-up,
you ugly freak!

107
00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:39.850
Don't you have a heart? I'm a
brilliant artist, you big jerk!

108
00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:41.350
I don't have time to
mess around with your

109
00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:43.620
childish little tricks anymore.

110
00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:45.710
Tricks, huh? Not so fast!

111
00:07:45.710 --> 00:07:47.180
They aren't just tricks!

112
00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:49.010
Just wait until you see!

113
00:07:49.010 --> 00:07:50.780
Within my art there
lies the power

114
00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:53.750
of the greatest friendships
and the truest loves!

115
00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:55.600
Right, I get it.

116
00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:57.070
I see what you're planning now.

117
00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:59.200
[MR. 2]
We all need love! And friends!

118
00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:01.610
It really just isn't going to work, though.

119
00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:03.640
Now let's see you hurt me!
[yells]

120
00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:07.140
How could you do that?

121
00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:08.680
You just attacked
your little friend

122
00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:09.790
with the long nose!

123
00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:12.790
Well, then, clearly you
don't value friendship much,

124
00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:14.170
do you?

125
00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:15.740
You're a real idiot.

126
00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:17.360
No matter what you transform your face

127
00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:20.090
to look like, you're still only you.

128
00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:21.990
I'm not the kind
to be fooled by images

129
00:08:22.030 --> 00:08:23.660
and façades like that.

130
00:08:25.330 --> 00:08:28.700
No way! A person is their soul!

131
00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:32.370
[MR. 2 whimpering]

132
00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:34.410
Is their soul?

133
00:08:36.090 --> 00:08:37.430
That's so...

134
00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:38.900
Wow!

135
00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:40.500
[crying]

136
00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:42.600
I am so embarrassed to
have been so caught up

137
00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:44.270
with appearances!

138
00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:47.910
I understand,
even if I was to become...

139
00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:48.940
...her, for instance.

140
00:08:48.940 --> 00:08:51.540
It wouldn't make any
difference to you at all,

141
00:08:51.580 --> 00:08:53.440
because images don't matter.

142
00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:03.310
[MR. 2]
Well, he's easy to read...

143
00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:07.720
You are such a fool.

144
00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:14.240
<b>Alubarna Palace</b>

145
00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:10.290
[ROYAL SOLDIER I]
– What?
[ROYAL SOLDIER A]
– It's Vivi!

146
00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:12.860
[ROYAL SOLDIER B]
It's true!
Princess Vivi has come back!

147
00:09:12.930 --> 00:09:14.160
[ROYAL SOLDIER C]
But why now?

148
00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:23.840
But Princess Vivi, that's insane!

149
00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:25.750
We can't do something like that!

150
00:09:27.990 --> 00:09:31.090
What are you afraid would happen if we did?

151
00:09:31.180 --> 00:09:33.580
That the kingdom would simply die?

152
00:09:33.610 --> 00:09:35.180
You're wrong, it wouldn't.

153
00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:37.450
This palace is not Alabasta, after all.

154
00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:43.070
Alabasta is...

155
00:09:59.210 --> 00:10:02.680
It is the people who are
out there hurting each other.

156
00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:04.550
They're the ones who
made Alabasta a country

157
00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:06.500
in the first place!

158
00:10:06.530 --> 00:10:08.500
If there's any chance
at stopping this war,

159
00:10:08.590 --> 00:10:10.090
then we must take it.

160
00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:12.500
Please, Chaka!

161
00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:14.670
We only need to draw
everyone's eyes over here

162
00:10:14.700 --> 00:10:16.370
for a few seconds!

163
00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:20.980
If you can do that, then I will take it from there!

164
00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:22.910
I swear, I can do this!

165
00:10:29.050 --> 00:10:33.220
[VIVI]
For now, please,
destroy this palace!

166
00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:42.630
[ROYAL SOLDIER A]
But you can't
be serious, Princess Vivi!

167
00:10:42.630 --> 00:10:44.870
[ROYAL SOLDIER B]
The palace has stood
in the same spot

168
00:10:44.900 --> 00:10:46.370
for four thousand years!

169
00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:47.970
[ROYAL SOLDIER C]
Please don't go
through with this plan,

170
00:10:47.970 --> 00:10:49.210
Princess Vivi!

171
00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:52.140
[ROYAL SOLDIER D]
Chaka! You have to use
your best judgment!

172
00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:53.980
[ROYAL SOLDIER E]
The king isn't even here!

173
00:10:53.930 --> 00:10:56.750
You can't possibly do this without his approval!

174
00:11:01.150 --> 00:11:02.920
[CHAKA]
Sire! We must take action

175
00:11:02.950 --> 00:11:06.320
against the rebels quickly,
before it's too late!

176
00:11:06.320 --> 00:11:08.160
[COBRA]
This is not some little quarrel.

177
00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:10.900
If we strike first, they will strike back.

178
00:11:10.910 --> 00:11:12.960
Are you suggesting that
we attack our citizens

179
00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:16.260
before we determine
who's behind all this?

180
00:11:16.290 --> 00:11:18.190
Because that would
be the true destruction

181
00:11:18.260 --> 00:11:20.060
of our kingdom.

182
00:11:20.090 --> 00:11:23.260
But we will act...
we will head out for Rainbase

183
00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:25.260
and Crocodile.

184
00:11:25.290 --> 00:11:27.230
[PELL]
Your Majesty,
attacking Crocodile now

185
00:11:27.260 --> 00:11:29.670
will only make things worse!

186
00:11:29.760 --> 00:11:32.590
It will only add fuel
to the rebel army's fire!

187
00:11:32.660 --> 00:11:34.360
If we leave for Rainbase now,

188
00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:36.160
the rebel army will
use our absence

189
00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:38.600
as a perfect chance
to attack the palace.

190
00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:40.400
[COBRA]
It doesn't matter
if the rebel army

191
00:11:40.430 --> 00:11:42.400
destroys this palace completely.

192
00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:44.600
It's only a building.

193
00:11:44.610 --> 00:11:45.520
You see,

194
00:11:45.520 --> 00:11:47.590
even if our royal army
does fall in the end,

195
00:11:47.620 --> 00:11:49.360
if we can just defeat Crocodile,

196
00:11:49.420 --> 00:11:51.490
this country can still
be reborn as long as

197
00:11:51.530 --> 00:11:53.930
its people are safe and whole.

198
00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:55.930
If we battle the rebel army instead,

199
00:11:55.960 --> 00:11:57.470
then that will all change.

200
00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:02.980
Remember...

201
00:12:02.980 --> 00:12:06.290
...the people are the country!

202
00:12:10.020 --> 00:12:11.160
[CHAKA]
Princess Vivi.

203
00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:16.190
[SOLDIERS gasp]

204
00:12:16.190 --> 00:12:18.500
[CHAKA]
I will do as you say!

205
00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:19.920
[NAMI]
You're just what they mean

206
00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:22.360
when they say "he's
nothing but talk."

207
00:12:22.390 --> 00:12:26.100
I bet you don't have enough
strength left to get up!

208
00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:27.060
[SANJI]
Don't think for a second

209
00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:29.630
that I'm just gonna
lie down and give up!

210
00:12:29.700 --> 00:12:31.440
You may look like Nami on the outside,

211
00:12:31.470 --> 00:12:34.600
but you're still the same
idiot on the inside!

212
00:12:35.890 --> 00:12:38.430
You bastard! I'll show you.

213
00:12:38.430 --> 00:12:38.910
[screams]

214
00:12:38.910 --> 00:12:40.580
I'm gonna...

215
00:12:41.910 --> 00:12:45.450
[laughing]

216
00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:48.450
[SANJI]
I can't do it! She's too cute!

217
00:12:48.490 --> 00:12:52.220
Oh, no! This desert air
is so stifling!

218
00:12:52.260 --> 00:12:55.490
It just makes me wanna rip all my clothes off!

219
00:12:55.560 --> 00:12:57.560
Ah! I'll help you!

220
00:12:57.600 --> 00:13:00.230
[NAMI]
Ballet Chop!

221
00:13:00.260 --> 00:13:01.730
Ow! My eye!

222
00:13:01.770 --> 00:13:04.670
Lovesick fool!

223
00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:14.470
[laughing]

224
00:13:14.470 --> 00:13:17.570
So! Nothin' but talk, are ya?

225
00:13:18.970 --> 00:13:20.670
I'll show you talk.

226
00:13:20.740 --> 00:13:21.640
[BON CLAY]
Hm?

227
00:13:21.670 --> 00:13:22.510
[chuckles]

228
00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:24.410
Nobody messes with me!

229
00:13:24.440 --> 00:13:28.350
Now, Mascara... Boomerang!

230
00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:29.980
[screams]

231
00:13:30.010 --> 00:13:31.540
Eat this!

232
00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:33.370
Please, don't kick me!

233
00:13:33.440 --> 00:13:35.180
[gasps]
Oh, no!

234
00:13:37.510 --> 00:13:38.780
Why?

235
00:13:42.350 --> 00:13:43.520
The "eyes" have it!

236
00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:45.320
[laughs]

237
00:13:45.350 --> 00:13:48.190
Well, this has been a treat,
but alas! I must be off.

238
00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:50.640
Duty calls, and I've got
a princess to kill!

239
00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:52.280
I really hate to rush things,

240
00:13:52.280 --> 00:13:55.080
but I'm gonna have to
finish you off now!

241
00:13:56.660 --> 00:13:59.830
Stand right there, lover boy, and I'll make this quick!

242
00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:00.900
Ha!

243
00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:05.200
Round and round and round
I go, and when I stop...

244
00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:07.580
[laughing]

245
00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:08.950
Wait a minute, did you just say

246
00:14:08.970 --> 00:14:11.310
we're supposed to blow
up the royal palace?

247
00:14:11.380 --> 00:14:12.280
I know that it sounds crazy,

248
00:14:12.350 --> 00:14:14.020
but those are the orders
that just came down

249
00:14:14.050 --> 00:14:15.090
from high command!

250
00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:18.390
[GUARD C]
We've been ordered
to blow up the palace!

251
00:14:18.430 --> 00:14:19.930
[GUARD D]
They can't be serious!

252
00:14:19.930 --> 00:14:23.770
[GUARD E]
That palace is 4000 years old!

253
00:14:23.770 --> 00:14:28.570
[SOLDIERS yelling]

254
00:14:28.600 --> 00:14:29.750
[CHAKA]
Nothing I can say

255
00:14:29.750 --> 00:14:32.850
can express my sorrow
at all of this.

256
00:14:32.910 --> 00:14:34.780
It's all right. I know.

257
00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:37.260
You really had no choice when
it comes right down to it;

258
00:14:37.260 --> 00:14:39.590
it was your duty to
intercept the rebel army.

259
00:14:39.620 --> 00:14:40.820
In spite of what
happened to Igaram,

260
00:14:40.890 --> 00:14:43.660
you've done well by managing
to keep the rebellion in check

261
00:14:43.730 --> 00:14:45.660
for the last two years.

262
00:14:45.730 --> 00:14:47.900
But... I wasn't wrong.

263
00:14:47.930 --> 00:14:52.680
I've met some true friends who
are going to save Alabasta.

264
00:14:52.680 --> 00:14:55.110
Once the royal army and the rebel army meet,

265
00:14:55.150 --> 00:14:58.950
this country, the Kingdom of
Alabasta, will be gone forever.

266
00:14:58.980 --> 00:15:00.780
If you are truly
the one and only hope

267
00:15:00.820 --> 00:15:02.850
for preventing that tragedy,

268
00:15:02.850 --> 00:15:05.690
then you must survive,
no matter what.

269
00:15:05.690 --> 00:15:09.190
So, from this moment forward,
what happens to Luffy,

270
00:15:09.190 --> 00:15:13.700
or any of us for that matter,
isn't the least bit important!

271
00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:18.140
[VIVI]
All of you, who were
willing to give your lives,

272
00:15:18.190 --> 00:15:19.730
how are you faring now?

273
00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:21.100
[CHAKA]
Princess Vivi.

274
00:15:21.160 --> 00:15:23.160
In the two years since
we've seen each other,

275
00:15:23.240 --> 00:15:26.070
you've grown into a
beautiful young woman.

276
00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:30.080
Once this war is behind us all,

277
00:15:30.100 --> 00:15:32.270
I'd like very much to hold a grand banquet

278
00:15:32.270 --> 00:15:34.740
to honor your pirate friends.

279
00:15:34.770 --> 00:15:36.270
Chaka.

280
00:15:38.140 --> 00:15:41.140
Okay, then give me food.

281
00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:43.750
After I beat up Crocodile,
give me food.

282
00:15:43.780 --> 00:15:46.120
I'll eat till I explode!

283
00:15:48.650 --> 00:15:51.090
[VIVI]
Yes. I believe in you, Luffy.

284
00:15:51.100 --> 00:15:54.310
You must be all right. You
must've defeated Crocodile.

285
00:15:54.370 --> 00:15:56.270
[door opens]

286
00:15:56.270 --> 00:15:57.810
My lord Chaka!

287
00:15:57.810 --> 00:15:59.510
Yes, report.

288
00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:02.380
Is it really true that they're
gonna blow up the royal palace?

289
00:16:02.430 --> 00:16:04.760
The soldiers are getting explosives ready.

290
00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:06.300
Surely this must be a mistake!

291
00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:09.300
There's no mistake, gentlemen.
That order was given by me.

292
00:16:09.300 --> 00:16:10.570
[BOTH gasp]
Princess Vivi!

293
00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:13.840
Use every ounce of explosives
that you can lay your hands on.

294
00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:16.110
The only way to stop this senseless fighting,

295
00:16:16.140 --> 00:16:19.150
and to save the lives of
the people of Alabasta,

296
00:16:19.150 --> 00:16:22.120
is to blow up the royal palace.

297
00:16:25.510 --> 00:16:26.410
What's this?

298
00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:27.840
[BON CLAY]
Ballet Kenpo!

299
00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:30.880
Memoirs of a Summer's Day!

300
00:16:30.910 --> 00:16:33.720
I see your weakness.

301
00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:37.220
There's a flaw in your attack.

302
00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:38.850
[BON CLAY]
Memoirs of a Summer's Day!

303
00:16:38.880 --> 00:16:40.650
[SANJI]
Joue Shoot!

304
00:16:45.320 --> 00:16:47.720
Sure enough, I was right.

305
00:16:47.790 --> 00:16:50.730
You've seen through it,
you say? Through what?

306
00:16:50.790 --> 00:16:53.860
What part of my ability could a
philistine like you appreciate,

307
00:16:53.900 --> 00:16:55.660
let alone see through?

308
00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:56.670
Only this.

309
00:16:56.670 --> 00:16:58.740
That you can't use your
precious Ballet Kenpo

310
00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:00.640
while you're assuming
Nami's form.

311
00:17:00.670 --> 00:17:02.170
[grunts]

312
00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:05.240
It's true, I can't bring
myself to attack you

313
00:17:05.310 --> 00:17:06.520
while you look like Nami,

314
00:17:06.550 --> 00:17:09.180
but it's pretty clear you have
to return to your normal self

315
00:17:09.220 --> 00:17:11.520
before you try to attack me.

316
00:17:11.570 --> 00:17:13.700
And it happens whenever
I see you touch your cheek

317
00:17:13.740 --> 00:17:15.740
with your left hand.

318
00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:20.950
[BON CLAY laughing]

319
00:17:21.010 --> 00:17:24.720
Eh? What? I can't hear you!

320
00:17:24.760 --> 00:17:26.860
Hey! I'm right, aren't I?

321
00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:30.770
Well... Well, so what
if you are right, pal?

322
00:17:30.800 --> 00:17:31.800
All right, all right.

323
00:17:31.870 --> 00:17:34.300
It's only with this magnificent
godlike physique

324
00:17:34.370 --> 00:17:35.540
that I've patiently developed,

325
00:17:35.570 --> 00:17:38.370
putting in day after day of
rigorous and brutal lessons,

326
00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:40.520
that I am able to perform
my Ballet Kenpo.

327
00:17:40.520 --> 00:17:41.730
But so what?

328
00:17:41.760 --> 00:17:45.000
You're still plenty black and
blue, aren't you, Mr. Big Talk?

329
00:17:45.030 --> 00:17:49.370
Now, take a look at
the prima of Ballet Kenpo!

330
00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:51.700
I'll say this much about it, then you're dead.

331
00:17:51.700 --> 00:17:55.770
The one on your left is the pen
and on your right is the cob.

332
00:17:55.870 --> 00:17:56.910
[SANJI]
Who cares?

333
00:17:56.910 --> 00:17:58.640
[laughs]

334
00:17:58.680 --> 00:18:00.850
Whether you see through it
or not doesn't matter!

335
00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:03.350
Now! Prepare to die!

336
00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:06.360
Behold the power of
my Ballet Kenpo!

337
00:18:06.390 --> 00:18:08.320
Bombardier!

338
00:18:12.260 --> 00:18:15.360
[SANJI]
What? He punched
a hole in the wall!

339
00:18:15.390 --> 00:18:17.420
[laughing]

340
00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:19.730
You dodged it! Smart thinking!

341
00:18:19.760 --> 00:18:23.500
At the end of their bent
necks are steel beaks!

342
00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:26.540
[SANJI]
He didn't even crack
the plaster around the hole!

343
00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:28.580
True power, when
compressed and focused

344
00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:30.520
into a single point of contact,

345
00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:32.710
will not destroy anything needlessly.

346
00:18:32.720 --> 00:18:35.220
It might be best if you were to
try thinking of one of my kicks

347
00:18:35.260 --> 00:18:37.560
like a shot from a
high-powered rifle.

348
00:18:37.590 --> 00:18:38.620
Of course, in this case,

349
00:18:38.690 --> 00:18:41.360
the bullets are of a drastically higher caliber.

350
00:18:41.400 --> 00:18:43.860
I'm going to perforate you!

351
00:18:43.920 --> 00:18:45.590
Un!

352
00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:46.590
Deux!

353
00:18:46.590 --> 00:18:48.490
Collier.

354
00:18:49.800 --> 00:18:51.330
No good!

355
00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:57.740
[SANJI]
Damn! His reach
is longer than mine!

356
00:18:57.770 --> 00:18:59.670
[laughing]

357
00:18:59.760 --> 00:19:01.630
Looks like the fight is over!

358
00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:04.330
I'm flying like a swan!

359
00:19:04.360 --> 00:19:09.340
Ballet Kenpo!
Memoirs of a Winter Sky!

360
00:19:11.010 --> 00:19:12.340
[SANJI]
But the longer his reach is,

361
00:19:12.380 --> 00:19:15.010
the longer it takes him to recover.

362
00:19:17.180 --> 00:19:18.650
If I can avoid his kick,

363
00:19:18.680 --> 00:19:20.520
I'll have that much more time to attack.

364
00:19:20.550 --> 00:19:22.850
[BON CLAY]
Say good-bye!

365
00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:28.190
[laughs]

366
00:19:28.850 --> 00:19:29.550
And just what do you think
you're gonna do now, lover boy?

367
00:19:30.620 --> 00:19:33.030
Hey, something's stuck to your left cheek.

368
00:19:33.060 --> 00:19:35.560
Huh? Really?

369
00:19:35.600 --> 00:19:37.700
Basses... Cote!

370
00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:42.700
[SANJI]
Longe!

371
00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:45.070
Tendron!

372
00:19:45.100 --> 00:19:47.210
[growls]

373
00:19:47.240 --> 00:19:48.040
Flanchet!

374
00:19:48.070 --> 00:19:50.580
Un!

375
00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:51.640
[groans]

376
00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:52.910
[chuckles]

377
00:19:52.910 --> 00:19:53.950
Deux!

378
00:19:53.980 --> 00:19:55.550
[BON CLAY]
– Ora!
[SANJI]
– Quasi!

379
00:19:56.580 --> 00:19:59.440
– Collier! Flanchet! Cuisseau!
– Un! Deux! Krah! Un!

380
00:19:59.480 --> 00:20:03.420
– Jarret! Tendron! Quasi!
– Un! Deux! Krah! Un!

381
00:20:03.450 --> 00:20:04.880
[SANJI]
Collier!

382
00:20:07.750 --> 00:20:09.920
[yells]

383
00:20:09.960 --> 00:20:11.760
[SANJI]
– Jarret! Collier!
[BON CLAY]
– Un! Deux! Ora!

384
00:20:11.760 --> 00:20:14.560
– Quasi! Flanchet! Gigot!
– Un! Deux! Krah!

385
00:20:14.590 --> 00:20:16.930
– Selle! Queue! Jarret!
– Un! Deux! Krah!

386
00:20:16.960 --> 00:20:20.900
– Collier! Quasi! Flanchet!
– Un! Deux! Ora!

387
00:20:20.930 --> 00:20:26.070
[BON CLAY]
Un! Deux! Ora! Un! Krah!

388
00:20:50.660 --> 00:20:52.000
[BOTH yell]

389
00:20:52.030 --> 00:20:54.770
[BON CLAY]
Bombardier Arabesque!

390
00:21:18.720 --> 00:21:24.730
[screaming]

391
00:21:48.150 --> 00:21:50.720
I... I give up.

392
00:21:52.090 --> 00:21:57.260
You've gotta be kidding.
You mean you're still alive?

393
00:21:57.330 --> 00:21:58.230
What's the matter?

394
00:21:58.260 --> 00:22:00.200
All you have to do is turn into Nami again

395
00:22:00.200 --> 00:22:02.200
and I won't be able to finish you off.

396
00:22:02.240 --> 00:22:03.540
[BON CLAY]
Nonsense.

397
00:22:03.570 --> 00:22:06.070
I can't move, with
the shape I'm in.

398
00:22:06.110 --> 00:22:09.880
There's no point trying to avoid the outcome of this.

399
00:22:09.910 --> 00:22:12.040
I congratulate you.

400
00:22:12.070 --> 00:22:14.210
Now kill me.

401
00:22:15.040 --> 00:22:19.880
You may as well. Baroque
Works will do it anyway.

402
00:22:19.910 --> 00:22:23.000
Don't just stand there,
get it over with.

403
00:22:23.000 --> 00:22:25.710
Come on, finish me.

404
00:22:26.740 --> 00:22:28.810
[gasps]

405
00:22:28.880 --> 00:22:32.580
It was a good fight,
and beyond that,

406
00:22:32.620 --> 00:22:35.420
we don't need anymore
words, do we?

407
00:22:42.760 --> 00:22:44.560
[BON CLAY chuckles]

408
00:22:44.590 --> 00:22:46.090
[BON CLAY]
This is, without question,

409
00:22:46.090 --> 00:22:52.060
the deep respect that arises
between rival, but I won't cry!

410
00:22:54.500 --> 00:22:55.600
[SANJI]
Bye now!

411
00:22:55.600 --> 00:22:58.470
Oh, and I'm takin' back our
sharpshooter's goggles.

412
00:22:58.500 --> 00:22:59.270
[BON CLAY groans]

413
00:22:59.300 --> 00:23:02.170
[BON CLAY]
Well, he did finish me.

414
00:23:05.110 --> 00:23:06.640
[SANJI grumbles]

415
00:23:06.670 --> 00:23:09.980
I think I cracked a couple of my bones again.

416
00:23:09.450 --> 00:23:17.290
<b>Battle of Polka Street</b>

417
00:23:11.410 --> 00:23:17.290
<b>South Block, Alubarna</b>

418
00:23:13.200 --> 00:23:17.290
<b>Victor: Sanji</b>

419
00:23:15.250 --> 00:23:17.290
<b>Prize: A Little Camaraderie</b>

420
00:23:18.630 --> 00:23:23.470
<b>Alubarna Palace</b>

421
00:23:23.860 --> 00:23:26.790
Uh, everything is ready
as you ordered, Princess!

422
00:23:26.790 --> 00:23:29.000
[GUARD H]
Everything is set here, too!

423
00:23:33.970 --> 00:23:36.640
[VIVI]
This castle has been a part of Alabasta's history

424
00:23:36.270 --> 00:23:38.420
history for four thousand years.

425
00:23:36.670 --> 00:23:39.170
for 4,000 years.

426
00:23:40.640 --> 00:23:46.650
[VIVI laughing]
[KAROO squawking]

427
00:23:46.650 --> 00:23:49.750
[VIVI]
It's been a great
source of pride to me.

428
00:23:52.090 --> 00:23:54.220
[VIVI]
But if we destroy
the royal palace,

429
00:23:54.260 --> 00:23:56.190
the people will have to stop
fighting with each other

430
00:23:56.220 --> 00:23:57.690
and pay attention!

431
00:23:57.730 --> 00:23:59.660
I'll finally be able to
tell everyone the truth

432
00:23:59.690 --> 00:24:02.830
about this horrible conspiracy
in my own words!

433
00:24:04.830 --> 00:24:06.770
All right, light your fuses!

434
00:24:06.800 --> 00:24:08.170
[gasps]

435
00:24:13.740 --> 00:24:15.240
[yells]

436
00:24:15.240 --> 00:24:18.840
[screams]

437
00:24:18.910 --> 00:24:21.350
What is this?

438
00:24:26.750 --> 00:24:28.150
[VIVI]
You okay?

439
00:24:28.220 --> 00:24:33.990
It... was him.

440
00:24:34.020 --> 00:24:36.730
[CROCODILE]
We can't have this.

441
00:24:46.070 --> 00:24:49.070
That was rather treacherous on your part, wasn't it?

442
00:24:49.140 --> 00:24:51.240
Huh, Miss Wednesday?

443
00:24:51.310 --> 00:24:54.980
After all, my dear, this is about to be my house.

444
00:24:54.990 --> 00:24:56.720
No, I'll never let you!

445
00:24:56.750 --> 00:24:57.980
[gasps]

446
00:24:59.400 --> 00:25:00.430
[CHAKA]
Your Majesty!

447
00:25:00.500 --> 00:25:03.000
[VIVI]
Uh! Father!

448
00:25:04.400 --> 00:25:07.900
This is lovely. To
have a palace like this.

449
00:25:07.940 --> 00:25:10.870
[CROCODILE laughs]

450
00:25:10.870 --> 00:25:12.740
It's a marvelous place to look down

451
00:25:12.840 --> 00:25:16.340
on all the filth and rabble below.

452
00:25:16.340 --> 00:25:18.450
Where-Where is Luffy?

453
00:25:18.450 --> 00:25:19.780
Who's that?

454
00:25:19.780 --> 00:25:22.350
Oh, you mean Straw Hat?

455
00:25:22.380 --> 00:25:25.290
That miserable young rookie?

456
00:25:28.120 --> 00:25:31.190
My dear, he's dead.
